title: Venn Diagram
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki
tags: MermaidExample

A Venn diagram shows logical relationships and overlaps between sets of items using overlapping circles. Use it for skill mapping, responsibility overlap analysis, and set membership visualization. ''New in Mermaid 11.'' Uses `venn-beta`.

---

!! Basic example

```
venn-beta
    set A ["Backend"]
    set B ["Frontend"]
    union A,B ["Full-Stack"]
    text A
        "Python"
        "PostgreSQL"
    text B
        "React"
        "CSS"
```

$$$text/vnd.tiddlywiki.mermaid
venn-beta
    set A ["Backend"]
    set B ["Frontend"]
    union A,B ["Full-Stack"]
    text A
        "Python"
        "PostgreSQL"
    text B
        "React"
        "CSS"
$$$

---

!! Real-world example: Engineering team role responsibilities

This example maps three engineering roles by their exclusive responsibilities. All `set` declarations come before any `union` (forward references cause a parse error). Text blocks are placed in exclusive set regions only.

```
%%{init: {"venn": {"width": 600, "height": 400}}}%%
venn-beta
    accTitle: Engineering team role responsibilities
    accDescr: Venn diagram showing skill overlap between Backend, Frontend and DevOps roles

    %% ── Set declarations (must come before any union) ──
    set BE ["Backend"] :3
    set FE ["Frontend"] :3
    set DO ["DevOps"] :2

    %% ── Overlap regions ─────────────────────────────
    union BE,FE ["Full-Stack"] :2
    union BE,DO ["Platform Eng"] :1
    union FE,DO ["Site Reliability"] :1
    union BE,FE,DO ["Tech Lead"] :1

    %% ── Text in exclusive set regions only ──────────
    text BE
        "Python"
        "PostgreSQL"
        "REST APIs"
    text FE
        "React"
        "TypeScript"
        "CSS"
    text DO
        "Kubernetes"
        "Terraform"
        "CI/CD"

    %% ── Set colors ──────────────────────────────────
    style BE fill:#0d6efd, color:#ffffff
    style FE fill:#198754, color:#ffffff
    style DO fill:#fd7e14, color:#ffffff
```

$$$text/vnd.tiddlywiki.mermaid
