---

!! Syntax

```
venn-beta
    set ID ["Label"] :N
    set ID2 ["Label"] :N
    union ID,ID2 ["Overlap Label"] :N
    text ID
        "item in exclusive region"
    style ID fill:#hexcolor, color:#textcolor
```

''set'' declares a circle with a display label and optional relative size `:N`. ''union'' defines an overlap region — referenced set IDs must already be declared above (no forward references). ''text'' places labels inside a set's exclusive (non-overlapping) region only. ''style'' applies a fill color to a set or union.

|!Keyword|!Description|
|`set ID ["Label"] :N`|Declare a named set (circle); `:N` controls relative size|
|`union ID1,ID2 ["Label"] :N`|Declare an overlap of two or more previously declared sets|
|`text ID`|Add label items inside a set's exclusive region|
|`style ID fill:#hex`|Apply a background fill color to a set|

!! Tips

* Always declare every `set` before any `union` that references it — forward references cause a parse error.
* The `:N` size values are relative: `:3` makes a set visually larger than `:1`.
* `text` blocks label items in a set's exclusive (non-overlapping) area only; placing text inside an intersection region is not supported in `venn-beta`.
* `venn-beta` is still beta — syntax may evolve in future Mermaid versions.

